From: Codex <codex@openai.com>
Date: Thu, 20 Aug 2026 12:20:00 -0700
Subject: [PATCH] webconfig: copy client association uptime to EasyMesh

The monitor already calculates assoc_dev_data_t.last_connect_time as seconds
since the station associated, and the EasyMesh em_sta_info_t has the matching
last_conn_time field.  The associated-clients translator omitted the copy, so
the agent always received zero and could not report client connection uptime.

Copy the existing observation into the EasyMesh data model.  This is the
duration of the current association and naturally resets after a disconnect or
roam.

Upstream-Status: Pending

diff --git a/source/webconfig/wifi_easymesh_translator.c b/source/webconfig/wifi_easymesh_translator.c
index c5fd7ec..84d78f2 100644
--- a/source/webconfig/wifi_easymesh_translator.c
+++ b/source/webconfig/wifi_easymesh_translator.c
@@ -1463,6 +1463,7 @@ webconfig_error_t translate_associated_client_object_to_easymesh(webconfig_subd
                     memcpy(em_sta_dev_info->radiomac, radio_info->intf.mac, sizeof(mac_address_t));
                     em_sta_dev_info->last_ul_rate = assoc_dev_data->dev_stats.cli_LastDataUplinkRate;
                     em_sta_dev_info->last_dl_rate = assoc_dev_data->dev_stats.cli_LastDataDownlinkRate;
+                    em_sta_dev_info->last_conn_time = assoc_dev_data->last_connect_time;
                     em_sta_dev_info->retrans_count = assoc_dev_data->dev_stats.cli_RetransCount;
                     em_sta_dev_info->signal_strength=assoc_dev_data->dev_stats.cli_SignalStrength;
                     em_sta_dev_info->pkts_tx=assoc_dev_data->dev_stats.cli_PacketsSent;
